# Node's `vm` module is documented as not being a security mechanism, so a probe
# that runs an operator-authored synthetic-monitor script through
# `vm.runInContext(script, sandbox, { timeout })` has exactly one control: what
# the context object carries. oneuptime's `VMRunner.runCodeInNodeVM` puts a live
# Playwright `Page` in there, wrapped in a `Proxy` whose `get` trap returns
# `undefined` for the names in a module-level `BLOCKED_SANDBOX_PROPERTIES` set
# and `Reflect.get(target, prop)` for everything else.
#
# That is a denylist over a live object graph, and Playwright documents how short
# the graph is: `Page.context()` returns a `BrowserContext`, `.browser()` returns
# a `Browser`, `Browser.browserType()` returns a `BrowserType`, and the
# `BrowserType` reference lists five ways to get a browser process --
# `launch()`, `launchServer()`, `launchPersistentContext()`, `connect()` and
# `connectOverCDP()`. `launch({ executablePath })` runs an arbitrary binary. At
# e8e4ee3ff074^ the set named `browserType`, `launch`, `launchPersistentContext`,
# `connectOverCDP` and `newCDPSession`, so `page.context().browser()
# .browserType().launchServer({ executablePath: "/bin/sh" })` walked straight
# through it, as did `connect()` and the `_browserType` alias. Fix commit
# e8e4ee3ff074 adds `_browserType`, `launchServer` and `connect` to the set; the
# construct is present at the parent and the remediation at the fixed revision.
#
# Detection is a JavaScript module-scope binding,
# `sandboxHostObjectMemberDenylistOmitsBrowserProcessEntryPoints`, emitting the
# new `code.SandboxHostObjectMemberDenylistGap` (VYQL-INJ-271, CWE-749/CWE-184).
# It reads four facts, all of them documented API: the module runs script through
# `runInNewContext` / `runInThisContext` / `vm.runInContext`, it forwards reads of
# a wrapped object with `Reflect.get`, and it denies the two names that identify
# the Playwright traversal -- `browserType` and `launch` -- while naming neither
# `launchServer` nor `connect`. Each name is matched in the quotes a list entry
# carries, because a module-scope context carries the module's raw source and the
# vulnerable file's own comment explains the
# `browser.browserType().launch(...)` route in prose.
#
# Measured on `Common/Server` of both revisions, 817 TypeScript files,
# `timeout 180 ./bin/vyql scan --cache off --max-ram 6GB`, three runs each:
# 802 findings / 124 at or above high at e8e4ee3ff074^ and 801 / 123 at
# e8e4ee3ff074, identical across all three runs on each side, the single delta
# being VYQL-INJ-271 on `Common/Server/Utils/VM/VMRunner.ts`.
#
# Reachable set rather than a subtree sample for the collateral, because
# oneuptime is a 288MB monorepo: exactly one file in the whole tree carries a
# `node:vm` run call at all, and it is `VMRunner.ts`. Across the 210 other corpus
# checkouts, 177 files carry a `node:vm` run call, 32 of those also call
# `Reflect.get`, and none of the 32 carries a quoted `browserType` -- every one is
# a vendored bundle (LimeSurvey webpack builds, yarn 4.0.2 releases) above the
# scanner's per-file source cap, so the reachable set outside oneuptime is zero
# either way.
#
# Concepts considered before minting: `code.SandboxFacadeWholesaleMemberCopy` is
# the nearest neighbour, but its condition is a facade *populated by copying every
# own property descriptor* of the host object, and nothing is copied here -- a
# Proxy forwards reads and a name set refuses some, so its name and its evidence
# text would misreport this module. `code.Vm2HostCallbackBridge` describes a
# sandbox exposing host callbacks or globals while sandbox code runs, which is
# equally true of both revisions and so is not the defect, and its wording is
# written about vm2's `VM`/`sandbox` API.
# `code.IncompleteKeyDenylistGuardedReadPrototypePollution` and
# `code.SegmentedKeyDenylistBypassPrototypePollution` have the denylist shape but
# are about `__proto__`/`constructor` on plain objects and are vulnerable to
# prototype pollution, not code execution. `code.H2oJdbcDisallowedParameterDenylistGap`
# and `code.PickleUnsafeImportBlocklistGap` are denylist-gap concepts whose
# conditions name one product's parameter or import namespace rather than a
# sandbox's host-object graph. `code.CodeEval` is labelled on
# `vm.runInContext` at both revisions, so a sink label cannot separate them.

test "rank1492: a node vm sandbox forwards a Playwright page behind a denylist that omits the browser-process entry points"
  lang javascript
  file Common/Server/Utils/VM/VMRunner.ts
  expect VYQL-INJ-271
  expect_review code.SandboxHostObjectMemberDenylistGap
  code
  ```
  import vm, { Context } from "vm";

  /*
   * Block Playwright methods that can spawn processes or access internals.
   * Prevents RCE via browser.browserType().launch({executablePath:"/bin/sh"})
   * and traversal via page.context().browser().browserType().launch(...)
   */
  const BLOCKED_SANDBOX_PROPERTIES: ReadonlySet<string> = new Set([
    "constructor",
    "__proto__",
    "prototype",
    "browserType",
    "launch",
    "launchPersistentContext",
    "connectOverCDP",
    "newCDPSession",
  ]);

  function createSandboxProxy(value: unknown): unknown {
    if (value === null || typeof value !== "object") {
      return value;
    }

    return new Proxy(value as Record<string, unknown>, {
      get(target: Record<string, unknown>, prop: string | symbol): unknown {
        if (typeof prop === "string" && BLOCKED_SANDBOX_PROPERTIES.has(prop)) {
          return undefined;
        }
        return createSandboxProxy(Reflect.get(target, prop, target));
      },
      getPrototypeOf(): null {
        return null;
      },
    });
  }

  export default class VMRunner {
    public static async runCodeInNodeVM(data: {
      code: string;
      options: { timeout?: number; context?: Record<string, unknown> };
    }): Promise<unknown> {
      const { code, options } = data;
      const sandbox: Context = Object.create(null) as Context;

      if (options.context) {
        for (const key of Object.keys(options.context)) {
          sandbox[key] = createSandboxProxy(options.context[key]);
        }
      }

      vm.createContext(sandbox, {
        codeGeneration: { strings: false, wasm: false },
      });

      return vm.runInContext(`(async()=>{ ${code} })()`, sandbox, {
        timeout: options.timeout || 5000,
      });
    }
  }
  ```

